00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.830
The upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon, is based on George RR

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.740
Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.110
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:20.010
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.220
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:28.670
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:32.220
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.591
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the

00:00:37.591 --> 00:00:42.760
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.570
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
In other words, it covers events from Aegon's

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:52.460
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:57.630
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:03.210
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:08.780
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:14.550
But back to Aegon's Conquest. King Argilac
Durrandon, also known as Argilac the Arrogant,

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.750
was the last Storm King from House Durrandon,
the rulers of the Stormlands since Durran

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:25.810
Godsgrief, a legendary figure of the Age of
Heroes and founder of Storm's End, and until

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:30.189
the Conquest by Aegon I Targaryen.
And before we continue I wanna talk for a

00:01:30.189 --> 00:02:59.010
moment about fantastic sponsor of today's
video.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:05.030
The House Durrandon of Storm's End is a former
Great House of Westeros. It ruled over the

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:10.120
Stormlands until the War of Conquest. It also
held much of the Riverlands until they lost

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:16.220
them to House Hoare. The head of House Durrandon
held the title of Storm King. Their houses

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:22.330
words were "Ours Is the Fury“ and their
sigil was a crowned black stag on a gold background.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:27.760
Sounds familiar? Well, that’s because Aegon
Targaryen’s half-brother, Orys Baratheon,

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:33.730
took the Storm King’s seat, daughter, house
words and sigil for his own House Baratheon.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:39.629
The title of Storm King was held by an ancient
Durrandon kings, who ruled the Kingdom of

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:45.120
the Storm, most of which is now the Stormlands
and at one point included the Riverlands,

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.470
Crownlands and the eastern part of the Reach.
The first of the line was Durran Godsgrief,

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:55.349
the mythic first Storm King and the founder
of House Durrandon. Legend has it that he

00:03:55.349 --> 00:04:00.690
was married to Elenei, the daughter of the
sea god and the goddess of the wind, and was

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:05.130
the builder of Storm's End.
The Storm's End's construction was attributed

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:11.150
to Durran, a legendary figure of the Age of
Heroes, who earned the hatred of the sea god

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:16.500
and the wind goddess when he took Elenei,
daughter of the two gods, as his wife. In

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:23.339
rage, the two gods sent massive storms to
destroy Durran's keep. Durran defied the gods

00:04:23.339 --> 00:04:29.300
and built a larger and more formidable keep,
but it was also destroyed. Durran's seventh

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:34.529
keep, built allegedly with an aid of Bran
the Builder, withstood the rage of Elenei's

00:04:34.529 --> 00:04:40.129
parents and gained the name of Storm's End.
The Storm's End became the seat of the rulers

00:04:40.129 --> 00:04:45.580
of Stormlands, the Storm Kings, for millennia.
One of the mightiest fortresses on the entire

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:51.259
continent, Storm's End has endured many sieges,
but has never fallen to any attacker in its

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:56.129
millennia-long history. Its seaward wall is
80 feet thick

00:04:56.129 --> 00:05:02.599
with a 150 feet drop into the sea below. The
castle is said to be protected by spells woven

00:05:02.599 --> 00:05:08.919
into its walls that prevent magic from penetrating
its defenses. The Storm King during Aegon's

00:05:08.919 --> 00:05:15.569
Conquest and therefore the last King of the
Durrandon dynasty was Argilac the Arrogant.

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:21.789
Argilac was a warrior king and considered
to be old by the time of Aegon's Conquest.

00:05:21.789 --> 00:05:27.150
When he was a boy, King Argilac turned back
a Dornish invasion. Towards the end of the

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:32.479
Century of Blood, he joined the great alliance
against the tigers from Volantis and led a

00:05:32.479 --> 00:05:37.930
host into the Disputed Lands, marching against
an army from Volantis which was attempting

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:44.089
to retake Myr. Twenty years later, in the
Battle of Summerfield , he killed King Garse

00:05:44.089 --> 00:05:49.339
VII Gardener of the Reach. Harren the Black,
the King of the Isles and the Rivers, was

00:05:49.339 --> 00:05:54.649
nearing completion of his massive castle,
Harrenhal, and was said to be looking for

00:05:54.649 --> 00:06:00.589
more conquests. Argilac had grown afraid of
Harren and so he tried to forge an allegiance

00:06:00.589 --> 00:06:06.629
with Aegon Targaryen who was at Dragonstone
with his sisters and their 3 large dragons.

00:06:06.629 --> 00:06:12.529
It is believed he wanted to create a neutral
area serving to separate hostile forces between

00:06:12.529 --> 00:06:19.099
his kingdom and Harren's. The Storm King offered
to Aegon the hand of his maiden daughter,

00:06:19.099 --> 00:06:23.629
Argella in marriage as well as dowry lands,
although, much of the lands were in fact in

00:06:23.629 --> 00:06:29.619
possession of Harren the Black. Aegon refused,
and instead offered the hand of his best friend

00:06:29.619 --> 00:06:36.210
and rumored bastard brother, Orys Baratheon.
Argilac took this as a grave insult and had

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:41.569
the hands of the envoy cut off. He sent them
to Aegon with a message of "These are the

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:46.240
only hands you will receive". Aegon called
his banners and took counsel with them and

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:51.910
his sisters. As Aegon had been waiting for
an excuse to use his armies and dragons on

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:57.809
Westeros, this came in well. Then Aegon sent
ravens to the rulers of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:06:57.809 --> 00:07:02.719
He informed them there would only be one king
in Westeros. Those who bent the knee would

00:07:02.719 --> 00:07:08.740
keep their lands and titles, but those that
didn't he would destroy. King Argilac refused

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:13.709
to submit. Aegon then strategically placed
himself between the Kingdom of the Isles and

00:07:13.709 --> 00:07:18.619
the Rivers and the Kingdom of the Stormlands,
so that Argilac and Harren could not decide

00:07:18.619 --> 00:07:24.000
on who should take action against him. After
landing and proclaiming himself Lord of the

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.530
Seven Kingdoms, Aegon named Orys Baratheon
the Hand of the King and sent him with a huge

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:34.589
army and his sister Rhaenys on her dragon
to take the Storm's End. Although Orys was

00:07:34.589 --> 00:07:40.659
met with some setbacks, he continued to march
on Storm's End. King Argilac refused to be

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:47.089
trapped inside his castle-like King Harren
who was roasted by dragonfire inside his castle

00:07:47.089 --> 00:07:54.189
walls, so he came out to meet the invaders.
He attacked Orys's forces while a huge storm

00:07:54.189 --> 00:07:59.039
raged, in what became known as the Last Storm
which resulted with the fall of the Kingdom

00:07:59.039 --> 00:08:05.830
of the Storm and the foundation of House Baratheon.
Argilac outnumbered Orys's army two-to-one.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:10.240
As the two armies closed on each other, a
massive storm, that would give a name to the

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:15.770
battle, broke out. Argilac, knowing he had
almost twice as many men as the Targaryens

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:22.099
and four times as many knights and heavy horse,
decided to press the attack. Three charges

00:08:22.099 --> 00:08:27.400
by Argilac's horsemen were slowed by mud,
although his spearmen had greater success

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:34.899
on foot and Durrandon host conquered two hills.
During the third charge Argilac broke through,

00:08:34.899 --> 00:08:40.469
but encountered Rhaenys atop Meraxes, who
destroyed their attack. By confusion, Argilac

00:08:40.469 --> 00:08:46.190
was thrown from his horse and found himself
face to face with Orys Baratheon. Both took

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:52.959
a wound, but soon Argilac would get his wish
and would die fighting, slain by Orys Baratheon.

00:08:52.959 --> 00:08:59.629
His death ended the battle, as the stormlanders
yielded or fled. After her father's death,

00:08:59.629 --> 00:09:05.529
Princess Argella Durrandon barred Storm's
End and declared herself Storm Queen. Her

00:09:05.529 --> 00:09:10.490
garrison, however, feared to share the fate
of Harren and revolted against Argella after

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:17.029
a few days, delivering her to Orys, chained
and naked. Nevertheless, Orys treated her

00:09:17.029 --> 00:09:23.269
gently, removing the chains, covering her
with his cloak and giving her food and wine.

00:09:23.269 --> 00:09:28.550
Afterward, Orys married Argella and became
Lord Paramount of the Stormlands. He took

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:35.210
the castle, lands, sigil and words of House
Durrandon for his own family, House Baratheon.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:41.060
Argilac got his nickname for arrogantly refusing
Aegon's offer of marrying Orys (a bastard)

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:46.649
to his daughter, cutting off the hands of
Aegon's envoy and sending them back to him.

00:09:46.649 --> 00:09:51.990
He was also arrogant in engaging the Targaryens
in open battle rather than withstanding a

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:58.079
siege in the infamously impregnable castle
of Storm's End. However, Argilac was motivated

00:09:58.079 --> 00:10:04.589
in this by having heard of the death of Harren
Hoare in similar circumstances at Harrenhal,

00:10:04.589 --> 00:10:09.600
who prepared for a siege in his immense castle
only for the Targaryen dragons to fly right

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:15.959
over the walls and burn him inside. If Argilac
resisted a siege by Orys, it would only be

00:10:15.959 --> 00:10:21.009
a matter of time until the Targaryens directed
their dragons to the castle, so wishing to

00:10:21.009 --> 00:10:26.769
avoid this fate Argilac met Orys in an open
battle. The last Storm King might have been

00:10:26.769 --> 00:10:32.440
a bit arrogant, but he was no coward, but
a true warrior. He's called arrogant for refusing

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:38.370
Aegon's proposal and for fighting Targaryens,
but on the other hand, the King in the North,

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:44.139
Torrhen Stark is called the King Who Kneeled
because he did not fight the Targaryens, but

00:10:44.139 --> 00:10:50.930
rather kneeled to Aegon, prioritizing his
people over his ego. So whichever option the

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:57.220
Storm King had chosen, he would have still
had an undesirable nickname and he was a born

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:04.139
warrior, so death by fighting a war was his
best choice. Aegon's Conquest, the Storm King,

00:11:04.139 --> 00:11:09.730
King in the North, many epic battles, all
of this is part of Fire And Blood, the long

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:14.449
Targaryen history, and the upcoming Game of
Thrones prequel, House of the Dragon is based

00:11:14.449 --> 00:11:20.310
on the Targaryen history. We are bound for
an epic journey starting in 2022 which is

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:24.839
when the first episode of the Game of Thrones
prequel airs. Thank you so much for watching,

00:11:24.839 --> 00:11:28.410
if you enjoyed this video please give it a
big thumbs up and I hope to see you in the

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:34.370
next one, peace!

